# Defence in depth behind vercel.json's outputDirectory: "site".
#
# A CLI deploy uploads the working directory, not the git tree, so .gitignore
# does not protect anything here. If outputDirectory were ever wrong or absent,
# these are the files that would become publicly fetchable.
#
# LEADING SLASH MATTERS. These patterns follow .gitignore semantics, where an
# unanchored "data/" would match site/data/ as well and take the deployed JSON
# with it. "/data/" matches only the repo-root working directory.
# site/ and everything in it — including site/data/organizations.json and
# site/robots.txt — is deliberately NOT listed here.

/source-reports/
/data/
/qa/
/prompts/
/docs/
/schema/
/scripts/
/.claude/
/CLAUDE.md
/README-START-HERE.md

# .env.local holds a live VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN. Git ignores it; Vercel would not.
.env
.env.*
